{
 "_meta": {
  "what": "The DAILY QUEST row set. GENERATED by harness/gen_daily_quests.py -- do not hand-edit.",
  "recovered": "the ids, the names, the detail sentences, the localisation keys and the target counts (parsed out of those shipped sentences) are [FFBEWW] data, from the three shipped localized-text tables F_TEXT_DAILY_QUEST_NAME / _DETAIL / _DES",
  "authored": "`reward_info` and `type`. No shipped table holds a daily-quest row: there is no F_DAILY_QUEST_MST in the GL corpus (219 tables) nor in the 98 JP/Memorial tables whose tokens match ours, so the definitions were server-side in both editions and we hold no copy. `type` is our reading of an icon index (sq_quest_type1..5.png, five frames across two atlases) -- LOW confidence until a run shows the icons.",
  "servable_rule": "an id needs BOTH a name row and a detail row, because the client builds MST_DAILY_QUEST_NAME_<id> and MST_DAILY_QUEST_DETAIL_<id> from the id (getName 0x1945404 / getDetails 0x1945524) and DISCARDS the Name/Details wire columns (their setters 0x1945520 / 0x1945640 are a bare `ret`)",
  "kind_note": "kind 30 = gil written `30:<amount>` and kind 50 = lapis written `50:1:<amount>`, which is how the SHIPPED schedules write them (F_LOGIN_BONUS_TOTAL_REWARD_MST `30:10000`, F_LOGIN_BONUS_SP_REWARD_MST `50:1:300`). A currency row's amount is read from `id` when there is no `count`, so `30:20000:1` RENDERS as '20000 Gil' and PAYS 1 gil -- verified by a claim. kind 21 = equipment, which routes to inventory.equipment (`unit_equip_display.md`)",
  "milestone_reward": "50:1:300",
  "milestone_note": "the DES-only ids (6000001-3, 6500001-9, 75000001-6) are the 'complete N daily quests' completion tiers; MST_DAILY_QUEST_DES_ does not exist as a string in libgame.so, so nothing in v9.0.0 builds those keys",
  "counts": {
   "name_rows": 50,
   "detail_rows": 185,
   "des_rows": 63,
   "name_and_detail": 46,
   "servable": 43,
   "unparsed_target": 0,
   "named_but_unpooled": 3
  },
  "unparsed_target_ids": [],
  "named_but_unpooled_ids": [
   "6000001",
   "6000002",
   "6000003"
  ],
  "named_but_unpooled_note": "ids with BOTH a name and a detail row that fall in no pool range, so they are servable in principle and unserved here. They are the DETAIL-only numbering families (1000/1001/1100/1200 style ids, e.g. 'Complete 7 daily quests', 'Perform 1 or more summons', 'Start an expedition') -- a different id space from the 6xxxxxx/7xxxxxx row families, so whether the server ever sends them is OPEN. Recorded, not guessed."
 },
